# HanBuy Project Rules

## Authentication & Security
- Frontend sends plain text password (NEVER hash on frontend)
- Backend uses bcrypt.compare(plainPassword, password_hash) for verification
- Backend field name is `password_hash` (NOT `password`)
- NEVER return password_hash in API responses
- Always normalize email: email.toLowerCase().trim()
- Always trim password before comparison
- Token expires in 7 days
- Add Authorization: Bearer ${token} header to all protected requests

## API Response Format
- Success: { success: true, user: {...}, token: "..." }
- Error: { success: false, error: "...", message: "..." }
- User object NEVER includes password_hash
- Products: { success: true, data: [...], pagination: { page, limit, total, totalPages, hasNextPage, hasPrevPage } }

## API Endpoints

### Authentication
- POST /api/auth/login - Body: { email, password } (plain text)
- POST /api/auth/logout - Headers: Authorization: Bearer {token}
- POST /api/auth/set-password - Utility endpoint

### Products
- GET /api/products/onhand?page=1&limit=50&category=...&brand=...&search=...&min_price=...&max_price=...&in_stock=true&sort=price_asc
- GET /api/products/preorder?page=1&limit=50&category=...&brand=...&search=...&min_price=...&max_price=...&sort=price_asc

### Query Parameters
- page: 1-1000 (default: 1)
- limit: 1-100 (default: 50)
- category, brand, search: optional strings
- min_price, max_price: optional numbers
- in_stock: optional boolean (onhand only)
- sort: price_asc|price_desc|name_asc|name_desc|created_desc|created_asc|stock_desc

### Pagination
- Always check pagination.hasNextPage and pagination.hasPrevPage
- Show page numbers using pagination.totalPages

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript
- Use async/await (not .then())
- Handle errors with try/catch
- Use meaningful variable names
- Add minimal logging (console.log for debugging only)
- **ALWAYS use `undefined` instead of `null` for optional fields** - This prevents TypeScript build errors. Use `undefined` for all optional properties, even if the type allows `null`.

## File Structure
- Services: src/services/
- Hooks: src/hooks/
- Components: src/components/
- Types: src/types/
- Utils: src/utils/

## API Client
- Use apiClient from @/lib/apiClient
- Base URL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL || 'https://hanbuy-api.onrender.com/api'
- Token stored in localStorage as 'hanbuy_token'
- User stored in localStorage as 'hanbuy_user'
- Always include Content-Type: application/json header

## Error Handling
- 401: Invalid credentials → Show "Invalid email or password"
- 403: Account not approved → Show approval message
- 400: Validation error → Show specific field errors
- 500: Server error → Show generic error message

## CORS
- Allowed origins: localhost:3000, localhost:3001, han-b-uy.vercel.app, .onrender.com, .railway.app
- Credentials: enabled
- Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, OPTIONS

## Don't
- Don't create documentation files unless explicitly asked
- Don't hash passwords on frontend
- Don't return password_hash in responses
- Don't log passwords or password hashes
- Don't use .then() chains (use async/await)
- **Don't use `null` for optional fields - ALWAYS use `undefined`** - Using `null` causes TypeScript build errors

## Do
- Fix code directly
- Normalize emails
- Trim passwords
- Handle all error cases
- Store token and user after login
- Clear storage on 401 errors
- Use pagination for large lists
- Check Cache-Control header for caching

